    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "BROWN 1 DET\nLENGTH OF KEEL\nLENGTH ON DECY\nTERRY AUDITI\n(from knight beads to taffrail\nFEET\nand meding to and of ungram in the you 1852 by A Can in the Clad Off of the Sued Cand of Name Yod\nI. Donald Mo Kay oog, builder of the Magnificent\nCLIPPER SHIP \"SOVEREIGN OF THE SEAS\".\nThis print is respoctfully dodicated buy the Publisher.\nLITH RY NCIDDIED\nSXTREME ARRANTH AR DRAM\n2IA PER",
      "THE PRESiDENT\nSherry\nDubonnet\nCampari\nBloody Mary\n*TENERA T9\nManhattan\nTom Collins\nMartini\nIT/E 7-51=\nScrewdricer\n#m2007 \u003e9=-59x-\nYodka\nScotch\n#te 235\nBourbon\nXaNtE ^-*\nDry Vermouth\n#XM F91^-Ex\nMaitai\n#l7922071 7131\nWhiskey Sour\nCollins\nCanadian\nSake\n#AT-7\nYodka\nOUR SELECTiON OF WINES\nWhite — Pinot Chardonnay\nRed - Cabernet Sauvignon\nChampagne —Almaden Blanc de Blancs\nCointreau\nCrème de Menthe\n#Y -**\nDrambuie\nBénédicine\nalte -\n#H#Y ^*17*1=\nCognac VIOP\nBénédictine and Brandy\n==+)\" (VSO P)\n#0**71771/277171",
      "SPECiAL\nHORS D'OEUVRE\nSpecialties from Various Countries\nFISH\nFillets of Sole Meuniere\nENTREES\nRoast Sirloin of Beef\nB F447\nGrenadins of Yeal with Tarragon Sauce\nCornish Hon stuffed with Wild Rice\nGrilled Lamb Chops\nMY 3\nCurried Breast of Chicken\nButtered Garden Vegetables\nStuffed Potato \"Mousseline\"\nDemitasse\nPilaff Rice\n10 2-57 • 31z\nCHEESE\nSelection of Cheese\nDESSERT\nPeaches in Cognac Sauce - Yanilla See Cream\nFruit Basket\n4:*\nAmerican\nCoffee\nCookies\nOrango Pekoe Tea Japanese\nHANT\nPAN AMERiCAN CUiSiNE BY MAXiM'S OF PARiS\n\"GOOD FOOD IS THE BASIS\nFOR\nTRUE\nA. Escoffier\n32610405\nGreen Tea\n#***",
      "CLIPPER SHIP \"SOVEREIGN OF THE SEAS\"\nThe front cover of this menu is a reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives clipper ship print.\nCurrier \u0026 Ives, known as the \"Printmakers of America\", graphically preserved the glorious clipper\nship era in a magnificent series of clipper ship prints. This print, one of a series, is being reproduced\nthrough the courtesy of The Museum of the City of New York.\nThe clipper ship \"Sovereign of the Seas,\" launched in 1852, influenced the design of all future\nclippers. She was built with almost a flat bottomed hull to allow for greater cargo carrying capacity,\nwhile maintaining speed. Many of the world's ship builders claimed that this was impossible to\nachieve. On her maiden run to San Francisco, with a mainmast that reached over 200 feet into the\nsky, and able to carry more than 12,000 yards of canvas, she made San Francisco in 103 days. To\nreport such record speeds was considered fantastic and incredible. It convinced the most skeptical\nof the value of flat bottoms for speed. On her maiden voyage, one of the passengers wrote in his\ndiary, \"It was fearful to see the topmasts bend as she beat around the Horn. We hardly dared look\naloft lest we should see the canvas blown away.\" To cap it off she then broke the record from\nNew York to Liverpool, making the run in 13 days, 13½ hours. \"Sovereign of the Seas\" reported\nthe highest rate of speed ever achieved by a sailing ship22 knots. The fastest of today's ocean\nliners steam along at about 31.5 knots.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers* of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the lanes of com-\nmerce to all the far places of the world... to Japan... to Australia... and, in the days of the great\ngold rush, from America's east coast, around Cape Horn, South America, to California. Our current\nequipment... the Clipper fleet of the Twentieth Century ... consists of the finest commercial\naircraft ever developed —aircraft that have helped us establish an unparalleled record for safety,\nsocca and service.\n•CUPPER TRADE MARK-RE\n2011.130.006\nSIN WORIN AIRWAYS INO\nLITHO IN USA -8739-0393"
    ],
